& [ArtifactAndQualityGate] passes at contract grade
  + twenty-four requirements map eligibility, profiling, realizations, interface, scheduling, correspondence, artifacts, admission, and target addendum
  + interpreter and native realization remain distinct
  + software semantic reference and profiling precede hardware
  + external technology correspondence informs the profile without selecting a tool or target
  + no artifact claims profiling, simulation, synthesis, timing, resources, bitstream, board, or device evidence

& [AuthorityGrant] is non-executable
  + future architecture and target evaluations must obey this eligibility and correspondence contract
  + profiling after the software reference may determine whether a target-specific source addendum is justified
  + this signature authorizes no HDL, HLS, compiler implementation, simulation, synthesis, netlist, bitstream, firmware, driver, board purchase, device access, loading, performance, or deployment
  + no future target activity begins without new preserved source, SJS signature, and separate claim

& [Invalidation] is fail-closed
  + any locked artifact drift
  + Process IR semantic change without reprocessing
  + effectful or unbounded kernel eligibility
  + target selection before profiling and addendum
  + interpreter and native evidence conflation
  + physical output match without semantic trace correspondence
  + procedure admission treated as bitstream or device admission
  + model-generated target artefact self-verification or self-loading
  + superseding source or signature protocol change

& [NextBoundary] is explicit
  + current FPGA profile is phase locked only as a non-executable contract
  + first permissible future work is software profiling and accelerator alternative comparison after software reference proof
  + target-specific hardware work remains blocked
